      "title": "Swiss voters reject stricter neutrality rules that would curb Nato cooperation",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/sep/27/swiss-vote-reject-stricter-neutrality-rules-nato",
      "description": "<p>70% vote against tightening centuries-old neutrality, which far right said was eroded by sanctions against Russia</p><p>Swiss voters have decisively rejected a proposal for a strict definition of neutrality that would have required Switzerland to curb cooperation with Nato and abandon sanctions against Russia.</p><p>All cantons and about 70% of voters rejected the proposal for a strictly defined version of neutrality to be ⁠written into the Swiss constitution, final results from the Federal Statistical Office showed. The motion had been promoted by the far-right Swiss People’s party (SVP).</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/sep/27/swiss-vote-reject-stricter-neutrality-rules-nato\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
